› Setup Q1

  Whether abcd's records (decisions, intents and issues, under .abcd/) are
  committed with your code or kept out of git, by abcd's block in .gitignore.

  Which answer does this repository take?

› 1. private
     records committed, shared by all who see the repository; only per-machine
     scratch, .abcd/.work.local/, is ignored. Suits unpublished code.
  2. public
     all of .abcd/ is ignored, so records stay on this machine,
     unpublished; so is memory/ at the top, abcd's older memory home.
  3. Decide later
     Leaves the value unset, so the install lists it again next time.

  Now: not set
  Change later: pass --visibility private|public to answer without asking
